# ── Clean URLs ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# /generhvervelse-aalborg/  →  generhvervelse-aalborg.php
# Any direct .php hit is 301'd to the clean URL so Google only indexes one
# version of each page.

RewriteEngine On

# 1. Redirect direct .php requests to the trailing-slash clean URL
RewriteCond %{THE_REQUEST} \s/+([^.\s?]+)\.php[\s?] [NC]
RewriteRule ^ /%1/ [R=301,L]

# 2. Add trailing slash where the .php file exists (e.g. /generhvervelse-aalborg)
RewriteCond %{REQUEST_FILENAME} !-d
RewriteCond %{REQUEST_FILENAME} !-f
RewriteCond %{DOCUMENT_ROOT}/$1.php -f
RewriteRule ^([^/]+)$ /$1/ [R=301,L]

# 3. Serve the .php file for the clean URL
RewriteCond %{DOCUMENT_ROOT}/$1.php -f
RewriteRule ^([^/]+)/$ $1.php [L]

# ── Caching for static assets ─────────────────────────────────────────────
<IfModule mod_expires.c>
  ExpiresActive On
  ExpiresByType text/css          "access plus 1 month"
  ExpiresByType image/jpeg        "access plus 1 year"
  ExpiresByType image/png         "access plus 1 year"
  ExpiresByType image/x-icon      "access plus 1 year"
  ExpiresByType video/mp4         "access plus 1 year"
</IfModule>

# ── Don't serve the mail config or partials directly ──────────────────────
<FilesMatch "^mail-config\.php$">
  Require all denied
</FilesMatch>

RewriteRule ^partials/ - [F,L]
RewriteRule ^phpmailer/ - [F,L]
